# .publish-denylist.example -- copy to .publish-denylist and fill in.
#
#     cp .publish-denylist.example .publish-denylist
#     git config core.hooksPath hooks
#
# One extended regex per line, matched case-insensitively against every file in
# every commit you push. A match refuses the push.
#
# `.publish-denylist` is gitignored, and that is the point: a list of the names
# you are trying to keep out of a public repo publishes those names the moment it
# is committed. This example file is tracked and holds no real ones.
#
# Keep it short. The list is a backstop for the structural checks in
# hooks/pre-push, not a substitute for reading the diff.

# The customer and the sending vendor.
# AcmeHealth
# Ingenio(us)? *Med

# Product and system names that identify the site rather than the standard.
# SomeRIS

# Accession, visit and account number shapes specific to your feed.
# \b13[0-9]{6}\b

# People. A radiologist's name in a note is still a name.
# Dr\.? +Lastname
